From 82b731fd64f107c90d04f7062a18d7bf5fac360b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brhett <36874370+jingledingle521@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:18:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 28/34] Finder file chooser: Finder-style Open/Save windows for
 xdg-desktop-portal

finder-filechooser implements org.freedesktop.impl.portal.FileChooser
(OpenFile, SaveFile, SaveFiles) with a window built from Finder's own
parts: its chrome (rounded, stoplights, glass sidebar, capsule toolbar,
folder title over a hidden path field), its sidebar, and Dolphin's view
with Finder's list and icon styling, plus Save As, file-type filters and
Cancel / Open along the bottom. Requests can be cancelled through the
portal's Request object. finder-extras/install.sh registers it (D-Bus
service, kde-portals.conf, and finder.portal in the system portal folder).

The window chrome now leaves column view, AirDrop and transfer cards to
Finder's own window, and the sidebar can hide AirDrop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KdkdNUmoM62iDwjRop6X5f
